  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "If three moles of an ideal gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> expand isothermally from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><msup><mi>dm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><msup><mi>dm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> against a constant opposing pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mi>kPa</mi></math>, then the amount of heat transferred is __________J.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1200",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kPa</mi></math></p><p>Using, first law of thermodynamics,<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔU</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> is the heat given or lost</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔU</mi></math> is the change in internal energy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> is the work done</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔU</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> : Process is isothermal</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mi>ΔV</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Irreversible</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the amount of heat transferred is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
